# Local agent instructions, not shared
CLAUDE.local.md

# Hand-off files used while pairing; never part of a change
_changes.patch
_commit_msg.txt

# Benchmark output. Runs against the local stack are cheap and repeatable, so the
# report is not a source of truth and is not kept.
#
# The contents rather than the directory: git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so ignoring `evaluation/reports/` would make the
# exception below a line that looks like it works and does not.
evaluation/reports/*
# A run against Azure is neither. It needs a deployed environment that exists for
# an afternoon and costs money, and the environment it measured is destroyed
# within the hour — so this one cannot be reproduced by running it again, and is
# committed for the same reason docs/measurements is.
!evaluation/reports/azure-*.json

# A deployment's running commentary, written by deploy.sh. It lives under
# docs/measurements because that directory is what the delivery workflow uploads
# as an artifact when a run ends — including a run GitHub killed, which is the
# only case where this file is the sole surviving account of what happened.
#
# Not committed, though. The measurements beside it are findings: reproducing
# them costs an environment and an afternoon, so they are kept. This is a
# transcript of one run's waiting, superseded by the next one.
docs/measurements/*-deploy.log

# Personal development journal, not part of the repository
NOTAS_DE_DESARROLLO.md

# The brief this project is built to. It is mine, it is written to an assistant
# rather than to a reader, and it is not part of what the repository is for.
CLAUDE_PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md
